Z||000000||speed racer||06-25-2001||12:15 PM||||Has any one tried the gtech that if so how accurate was it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||06-25-2001||01:35 PM||||They are very accurate. Not more than 0.1s or 0.2s off the real time. I know of many people (in a Vette forum) trying it at the track also with same results. They are very good to practice your launches for consistency.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||The Fieromaster||06-25-2001||01:38 PM||||Gtech is pretty good... I tested my Eclipse GSX when i had it 2 runs gave me a number of 215 horse power... My 1/4 mile run was screwed up by 3rd shift people walking across the road in the industrial development... oooopsie!  It seems acurate but to get the right 1/4 mile time you need the exact weight of you and your car, so take it to a wiegh station for closer numbers!<P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">    <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||06-25-2001||03:00 PM||||Fieromaster, I think what you are trying to say is that to get accurate HP numbers you need the accurate weight of the car. For normal 0-60, 1/4 mile, etc times you don't need the weight. It is just for HP calculations.<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bazooka||06-25-2001||06:28 PM||||Accuracy is good. The only thing I don't like is that it(the meter) has to be indexed and activated by hand immediately before each trial run. It gives 1/4 and 1/8 mile ET's, Horsepowers, and G-force readings. For $140 its unbeatable. There is also a deal at Discount Tires that you get the G-tech free with the purchase of a set of high speed tires. Check em out<BR>***************************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by speed racer:<BR><B>Has any one tried the gtech that if so how accurate was it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
